WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:09.360
There's no denying 2016 was a fantastic year
for video games, but 2017 is shaping up to

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.550
be even better.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:16.349
Here's a sneak peek at the top video games
of 2017.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.349
Winter

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:23.970
The year kicks off in epic fashion with the
January release of the hotly anticipated Resident

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:30.500
Evil 7, the latest entry in the franchise
which has been the industry standard in horror

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.260
for over two decades.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.329
And things don't slow down from there.

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:42.850
Winter also finally brings gamers For Honor,
which has been teased for seemingly an eternity

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.330
at this point.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:51.820
Then there's also the bizarre future dystopia
Horizon Zero Dawn and the latest Tom Clancy

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.360
game, Ghost Recon Wildlands.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.400
Plus real time strategy fans get a special
treat with the release of Halo Wars 2, while

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:11.320
fans of the superhero fighting game Injustice
finally get a sequel as well.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:17.540
But all of that is overshadowed by one of
the most hotly anticipated games of the year,

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:24.110
Mass Effect: Andromeda, which is set to blow
minds in March as the series leaves Commander

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:30.210
Shepard and the entire Milky Way behind for
a galaxy full of new characters, new aliens,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:35.750
and new moral conundrums sure to test even
the bravest of souls.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:44.700
Heck yeah!

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.700
Spring

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.560
Fans of the Persona series have waited nearly
nine years for the next official installment

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:58.380
to be released, but that wait will finally
end in April when Persona 5 hits consoles

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.619
with the story a new group of students at
Shujin High School who band together to face

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:05.760
down the shadowy group known as the Phantom
Thieves of Hearts.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.099
And Persona isn't the only series to get a
sequel in Spring.

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:15.990
Outlast II promises a new round of survival
horror and nightmare inducing creepiness,

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:21.750
while Tekken 7 is no doubt full of people
punching each other and shouting catchphrases.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:27.360
Gwent, meanwhile, takes the game-within-a-game
from the Witcher franchise and gives it the

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:33.360
full spotlight in a Hearthstone-style collectible
card game with a single-player campaign.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.410
Perhaps the most intriguing title of the Spring,
though, is Tacoma.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:44.340
Brought to you by the same minds who created
the surprise hit Gone Home, Tacoma takes that

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:50.310
game's investigative mystery feel and moves
it to the claustrophobic interior of a derelict

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:55.860
space station — where something has definitely
gone wrong.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:01.360
Players have to try and uncover the mystery
of what happened to the crew.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.580
Honestly?

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.930
It's so creepy already, we're not sure we
even want to know.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.239
Summer and Fall

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:13.860
Considering the gaming industry is full of
delays and outright cancellations, it's no

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:20.260
wonder studios are hesitant to give their
games firm release dates too far in advance.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.680
But while we don't know for sure when these
games are going to come out, here are some

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:30.060
of the other titles you should be able to
play sometime in 2017.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.830
Inspired by old Mickey Mouse cartoons, Cuphead
has captured the imagination of retro gamers

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.030
and sidescroller fans everywhere.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:45.060
Rumor has it the designers are just putting
the final touches on co-op mode, so no further

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.280
delays are anticipated.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.370
Besides Cuphead, there are a handful of other
new intellectual properties to keep an eye

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.790
on this year.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:59.950
Scalebound is an epic third-person action
game where you get to control a freaking dragon…

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:09.860
...which is always cool.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:15.430
Days Gone features more apocalyptic survival
fare, only this time in one of our nation's

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:19.350
national parks, so that's, y'know, nice.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:25.979
And Detroit: Become Human fights back against
urban decline with a futuristic neo-noir story

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:31.040
about androids, where every choice has major
ramifications for the storyline.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:38.210
If sequels are more your thing, though, don't
worry, because 2017 has a metric ton of returning

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.590
franchises, starting with God of War.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:47.790
Yes, Kratos is back in a story which sees
the older and more grizzled warrior taking

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:52.340
on a new challenge: osteoporosis.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.620
"I've fallen and I can't get up."

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.190
Ah-hah, no.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.729
Just kidding, he's fighting the Norse gods
and monsters this time.

00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:06.650
There are plenty of other fan favorite franchises
making a comeback in 2017.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:12.450
Shenmue 3 makes its long awaited return after
getting crowdfunded on Kickstarter.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:18.150
Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild takes
the Nintendo classic and adds a dash of

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.530
modern gameplay.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:27.160
Dead Island 2 moves the zombie survival game
to Los Angeles and focuses on slapstick multiplayer

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.160
gameplay.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.530
Quake Champions is the latest first-person-shooter
arena showdown.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:38.759
Agents of Mayhem is a Saints Row third person
shooter spin-off revolving around an anti-terrorist

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:40.070
organization.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:45.770
Crackdown 3 features an open world sandbox
and the ability to level civilizations with

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.820
godlike powers.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:53.301
Then there's also a Spider-Man game coming
from the developers of Ratchet &amp; Clank, which

00:05:53.301 --> 00:05:59.030
will no doubt somehow tie in to the release
of the summer film blockbuster Spider-Man:

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.270
Homecoming.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:07.350
And then there's Super Mario Switch, a game
so secret, we don't even know the actual title

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.350
yet.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.350
But wait!

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.350
That's not all.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.250
Two of the biggest releases of the year are
also sequels.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:19.310
South Park: The Fractured But Whole builds
on the surprisingly great RPG elements of

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:25.449
South Park: The Stick of Truth to deliver
an even broader and more detailed world, this

00:06:25.449 --> 00:06:28.920
time parodying the superhero genre.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:35.150
And the mere announcement that there would
be a Red Dead Redemption 2 was enough to rocket

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:39.590
the game to the top of everyone's wish list
for next Christmas.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:45.680
Here's hoping Santa has a huge sleigh, because
he's going to need it to carry all these great

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:46.680
games.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:47.680
Thanks for watching!

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.669
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:50.669 --> 00:06:53.339
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

